@scene(120)

// A threaded shaft end. An M10 x 1.5 thread at the left, chamfered where it
// starts so a nut finds it, and run out at its other end as a lathe tool
// retracts: the groove's floor rises in a straight line from the root to the
// major diameter, here over 2.5 pitches, into the plain neck beside it. Then a
// shoulder for the nut to seat against, and a journal. Every segment is placed
// by the two planes it runs between, measured from the left end. Lengths are
// in mm.

@range(0, 2) threadChamfer = 1.0;
@range(0, 8) runoutLength = 3.75;

threadedShaft = shaft.body(
  [shaft.thread(10.0, 1.5, 0.0, 20.0, shaft.chamferEnd(threadChamfer), shaft.threadRunout(runoutLength)),
   shaft.diameter(10.0, 20.0, 26.0),
   shaft.diameter(18.0, 26.0, 40.0),
   shaft.diameter(14.0, 40.0, 70.0)]);
threadedShaft.color = [0.58, 0.60, 0.64];

// Laid along X and centred, so the viewer frames the whole shaft.
laid = transform.translate(transform.rotateY(threadedShaft, neg(pi) / 2.0), [35.0, 0.0, 0.0]);
return laid;
